# Electron application,
## plattform/package
Initial supported desktop target: Windows x64.
Task 0204 must produce a locally runnable packaged Windows x64 Electron application. Installer/signing/publishing are explicitly deferred.
Electron Forge is the packaging tool unless repository inspection reveals an existing standard that should be reused.

## host ownership
Electron is a client and launcher, never the authoritative runtime owner.

On application startup:

1. Resolve the configured local A008 host endpoint.
2. Probe host readiness using the existing authenticated/local host contract.
3. If a compatible host is already running:
   → attach to it.
4. If no compatible host is running:
   → start the existing A008 GUI host as a separate local process.
5. Wait for host readiness.
6. Only then create/load the A008 GUI renderer.

The Electron renderer never starts, stops, leases, owns or directly
communicates with session workers.

A host process started by Electron must not be tied to BrowserWindow lifetime.
Closing or reloading the Electron window must not cancel accepted runs,
terminate session workers, release runtime ownership, or stop the host.

Electron may bootstrap the host, but host ownership remains defined by the
existing A008 host/platform lease and process model. Electron must not create
a second ownership mechanism.

Existing host wins.

Electron must not attempt to replace or restart a healthy compatible host.
If host startup reports that runtime/platform ownership is already held,
Electron must re-probe the configured endpoint and attach to the existing
owner when compatible.

# renderer-model
The renderer is the existing A008 GUI application.

It receives no Node.js capability.

BrowserWindow:
- nodeIntegration: false
- contextIsolation: true
- sandbox: true
- webSecurity: true
- no arbitrary navigation
- no arbitrary new-window creation

No preload API is added unless repository inspection proves the existing web client cannot perform a required desktop operation through the existing host contract.

## single-instance
Only one Electron shell instance per user profile is allowed.

A second launch must focus/restore the existing Electron window and exit.
It must not start another host or create another desktop ownership domain.

## Decisions and Notes
### Frozen Desktop Integration Decisions

- Initial supported desktop target is Windows x64.
- A008-0204 delivers a locally runnable packaged Electron application.
  Installer generation, code signing, publishing, auto-update and additional
  operating systems remain outside this task.
- Electron Forge is the default packaging mechanism unless inspection finds
  an existing repository-owned packaging standard that should be reused.
- Electron is a thin desktop client/launcher. It is not a runtime, session,
  memory, lease or accepted-work owner.
- The renderer is the existing `gui/` application and continues to communicate
  through the existing A008 GUI-host/client contract.
- On startup Electron first probes the configured local host. A healthy
  compatible existing host is reused.
- If no compatible host is available, Electron may bootstrap the existing
  A008 GUI host as a separate local process, then waits for verified readiness
  before loading the renderer.
- Host authority remains defined by the existing A008 host/platform ownership
  and lease model. Electron introduces no parallel ownership mechanism.
- A host bootstrapped by Electron must not be coupled to BrowserWindow
  lifetime. Closing/reloading the desktop window must not stop the host,
  session workers or accepted runs.
- Host shutdown semantics beyond the existing host contract are not introduced
  by this task. An explicit desktop "stop host" or lifecycle manager is a
  separate future feature.
- Only one Electron shell instance per user profile is allowed. A second
  launch focuses/restores the existing window and must not start another host.
- Renderer Node integration is disabled, context isolation and sandboxing are
  enabled, and web security remains enabled.
- No preload API is introduced unless a concrete requirement cannot be
  satisfied through the existing GUI-host contract. Any required preload API
  must be narrow, typed and explicitly allow-listed.
- Navigation and new-window creation are restricted to explicitly approved
  local A008 surfaces. Arbitrary external content is not granted Electron or
  preload capabilities.

### Primary Deliverable

A Windows x64 Electron desktop shell under `clients/electron` that packages and
presents the existing `gui/` client, discovers or bootstraps the existing local
A008 GUI host, waits for verified host readiness, and connects through the
existing client contract without becoming a runtime owner.

The packaged application must remain functionally equivalent to the web GUI
for shared features. Closing or restarting the desktop renderer must not cancel
or terminate host-owned accepted work.

### definitions of done
- Starting Electron while no host is running starts exactly one host and reaches
  a ready GUI.
- Starting Electron while a compatible host is already running reuses it and
  starts no second host.
- Closing/reloading the BrowserWindow during an accepted run does not stop the
  host, session worker or accepted run; reopening Electron reconnects to the
  durable state.
- Launching a second Electron instance focuses/restores the first instance and
  does not start another host.

  